WEBVTT

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:03.980
It has finally begun – the Pantasia newcomers’ battle.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.400
A young girl, Azusagawa Mizuno, appeared before Kazuma.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.110
She was Tsukino’s sister, but from a different mother.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.660
Melon bread has been decided to be the
theme for the first round of the finals.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.760
Mysteriously, Kazuma’s opponent in
the first round of the finals was...

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.060
Mizuno.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.270
Facing Mizuno, who wouldn’t address Tsukino as “nee-san,”

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:28.170
Kazuma proposed that if he was to win, she
would have to call her sister “nee-san.”

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:34.010
Thereupon, Mizuno suggested the following
if the opposite were to happen.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.950
That’s fine, I’ll do it.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.580
In exchange, if you lose,

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.930
I’ll have you come over to the New
Tokyo Branch as an employee.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.330
All right, then,

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:44.710
it’s a promise.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:46.020
Hey, Azuma!

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.590
Don’t decide things so easily.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.960
You don’t know anything about her skill...

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.630
Moreover, are you especially good
at making melon bread?

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.640
Hmm... I’m kinda bad at it...

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.510
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.350
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist..

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.640
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.000
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.320
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:17.910
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:35.150
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:43.120
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:51.000
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:58.710
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:06.180
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:15.560
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:24.320
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:28.580
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.540
is the light of only you.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.320
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:40.130
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:47.850
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.920
Sorry for the wait!!

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.470
Meron-meron with melon bread!

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.300
When you say you’re bad at it, you
mean that you’re bad at it, right?

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.490
Yeah, I’m bad at it.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:03.140
T-That’s not good!

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:06.390
Even now, I wonder if we can’t cancel this promise...

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:10.660
Ah! But considering her personality, it’s really, really...

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:13.770
What is it?

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.960
You think that I’d lose, Tsukino?

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.470
No, that’s not it, but...

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:21.490
Well...

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.290
I...

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.220
I don’t want to lose you, Azuma-san.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:30.790
Don’t worry.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.810
I’ll always be an employee at
the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.820
A-Azuma-san...

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.390
Naive!

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.320
At the New Tokyo Branch that Mizuno works at,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.510
they use the pulp from the highest grade muskmelon,

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:48.790
and have made a highly popular melon bread,
surpassing even that of the Main Store.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.190
The 12:00 p.m., 3:00 p.m., and 6:00 p.m. batches

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.400
are famous for being sold out
as soon as they are on sale.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.290
And they sell as many as 800 of them in a day!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.570
It’s not surprising for Tsukino to be worried.

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:03.300
I-Is it... really that popular?

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.280
I guess I really am worried.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.530
Azuma-san!

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:08.950
This is bad...

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.750
After making a promise like that,

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.310
we can’t really run away now.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:17.310
At this rate... Azuma will... really...

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:24.140
I’ll just intrude a little.

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:29.290
Ah! There he is!

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.600
Hey, kid! I was looking for you!

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.860
Actually, the other day...

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.610
W-Why? Why?

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.010
Did something bad happen?

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:42.740
Azuma Kazuma
Azusagawa Mizuno

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.510
So, that is... in other words...
Azuma Kazuma
Azusagawa Mizuno

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:49.450
If you lose the melon bread challenge
to that Mizuno girl,

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.250
the kid’ll have to move to another store.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.000
Is that the problem?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.130
Yeah.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:56.770
It’s a serious issue.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:59.040
Why, why?

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.090
Well then, it’s all fine if you win, right?

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:02.690
Yeah, but...

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.720
This moron’s bad at making melon
bread, which is the topic.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:08.890
Why?

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.510
Because, you see...
I don’t quite understand it.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.070
What melon bread is...

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.530
Why is it melon bread?

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.520
You moron!

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.760
Does this have anything to do with it at such a time?

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:24.900
That’s right, kid.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:29.620
Even I don’t ever wonder why cucumber
sushi’s called “kappamaki.”

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:32.580
But that has nothing to do with it, right?

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:37.120
The New Tokyo Branch seems
to be using real melon pulp.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:40.270
In that case, it wouldn’t be odd to call it melon bread.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.250
Should we also use fruit pulp?

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:44.780
That’s true, but...

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.760
Actually... Somehow, I...

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.050
can’t really like the bread itself.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.660
Yeah... it’s not like I don’t understand that feeling.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.600
Manager?

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.170
Melon bread is, so to speak, a <i>Japan</i>.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:03.320
Just like an-pan and cream-pan, if was born in Japan.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:06.190
It is, without a doubt, an original Japanese bread.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:09.530
However, on top of that, due to pressures in history,

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.180
there’s an incomplete portion which remains within it.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.180
An incomplete portion?

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.690
As you know, melon bread has cookie
dough covering the bread dough,

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:17.430
bread dough

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.960
cookie dough

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.190
and the two of them are baked together, just like that.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:25.380
But traditionally, in order to thoroughly
bake cookie dough,

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:27.800
you need three times the amount of
time you need for bread dough.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.090
In other words, with the present
manufacturing process,

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:34.060
if you bake it so as not to burn the bread dough, the cookie dough is left underbaked...

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.600
and if you bake the cookie dough well enough, then the bread dough will be burnt black.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:40.400
You can’t sell bread that’s burnt black.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.000
That’s why most bakeries sell melon
bread with the cookie dough

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.320
Melon-pan

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:46.630
on the surface underbaked, so as
not to burn the bread dough.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.340
This is the “incomplete portion.”

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:55.850
It’s true that the cookie dough portion of melon bread should be baked a little more...

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:02.790
If you were to eat it fresh from food carts, as
is popular in Kansai right now, it’d be fine...

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.050
But, if even a little time passes,

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:10.360
the underbaked cookie dough absorbs water,
and its consistency becomes sticky.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:14.720
If we were to find a way to conquer
that incomplete portion,

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:15.410
we might win!

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.060
Perhaps!

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:21.940
However, while our history in bread has not been long...

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:23.240
melon bread has been around

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:25.440
and has been acknowledged since the 6th year of the Showa period.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.320
It’s been about 70 years since then.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.200
It’s not an easy thing, as many an artisan has tried and

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.210
failed at giving birth to a method to fix this defect.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:36.170
70 years...

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.330
This is bad...

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:42.630
That dark atmosphere’s coming back...

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:46.920
There’s no point in thinking about
such gloomy things all the time...

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.940
I’ll cheer you up in a minute.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:56.470
Hey, kid! The other day, I couldn’t offer
you anything but wasabi, right?

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:59.700
It’s unacceptable to be thought of as stingy, so...

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.480
I have plenty of toppings and rice ready today.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.460
Don’t be shy and eat until you’re full, okay?

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.460
Here you go.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.300
Delicious!

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:15.300
De-licious!

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:16.490
Tuna!

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:17.080
Okay!

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:17.740
Hairtail!

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:18.370
Here you go.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:19.290
Note: Botan’ebi is a type of a shrimp that is very sweet.
Botan’ebi!

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:19.880
Okay!

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:35.930
What happened?

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.280
Is it not tasty?

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.790
It’s sushi!

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.500
Huh? Of course it is!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.790
It’s sushi!

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:46.650
Wh-What was that?

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:49.020
He seems to have gone off somewhere...

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:51.440
And how can you people be eating so calmly?

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:52.510
Is it okay to leave him?

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:53.650
Oh, yeah.

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.330
It happens all the time.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:59.030
In a way, when Azuma suddenly
runs off somewhere like that,

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.040
it’s okay to assume that everything’s all right.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.160
Is that so?

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.520
Sir, salmon roe, please!

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:07.520
Salmon roe...

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.180
Sir, one more!

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:18.470
Huh? Mizuno!

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.060
What are you trying to do?

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:23.410
It’s not good to have a monopoly
on delicious things, Tsukino-san.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.440
Y-You’re...

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.020
That’s why I’m going to have
you share Kazu-kun as well.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:31.130
I’ll gobble him up quickly,
just like the salmon roe.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:33.380
Like I’d let you do something like that!

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:40.010
This is payment for the salmon roe, okay?

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.370
This is...

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:46.020
The melon we usually use at the store.
Try eating it.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.630
Ah, but for tomorrow’s challenge,

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:51.520
I’ll be using one that’ll put this melon to shame, so...

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.670
with that in mind...

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:55.300
Bye, see ya tomorrow!

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:57.470
Let’s go, Koala!

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.770
Mizuno seems to be really confident, doesn’t she?

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:06.790
I’m sure that this melon is an absurdly delicious melon.

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:10.150
Tomorrow, they’ll challenge us with a melon
that’s much better than this one.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:13.150
In other words, this is a demonstration, right?

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:14.300
Let’s eat it and see...

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:15.870
All righty...

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.390
This melon even looks delicious.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.250
And this fragrance...

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:31.380
I can’t be patient anymore!

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:34.850
D-Delicious!

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.720
The moment you place it in your mouth it
melts, its sweetness spreading all over.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:42.350
This is the first time in my life that
I’ve had such a delicious melon.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.240
No!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.560
Don’t call this a melon!

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:46.410
The melons I’ve been eating so far have been...

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.150
Stop right there!

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:51.360
That was close...

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:56.330
Ah! A melon whose skin I almost ate...

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.170
Tomorrow’s melon is ever tastier than...?!

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.160
That’s impossible!

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.370
It’s not possible to stand up to such a delicious melon.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.890
We definitely can’t stand up to
them in terms of fruit pulp.

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:07.830
That’s right.
If Azuma wants to win,

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:10.460
he has to complete the incomplete
portion of melon bread...

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:12.400
No, there’s a way besides that...

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.220
Azuma-san!

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:21.450
Tsukino!

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:23.450
Y-Yes?

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:25.940
Please go out with me!

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:30.210
Huh? Y-Yes?

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.710
Gourmet Mart

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:34.710
I ended up going out with him, but...

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:38.450
Ah, umm... Azuma-san...

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:42.660
Umm... what are we doing here?

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:44.180
Could this really be...

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.680
What? Isn’t it obvious?

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:50.930
Could this really be a da... da... da...?

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.580
We’re shopping for ingredients.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:55.680
I forgot to bring money, so I had you come with me.

00:11:58.300 --> 00:11:59.420
Is that the case?

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.380
I don’t mind, but...

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:03.410
what in the world are you
trying to make?

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:05.100
<i>Japan</i>.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:08.080
<i>Japan</i> #58. Melon sushi bread!

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:08.970
sushi
melon

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:10.900
Melon sushi bread?!
sushi
melon

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:11.480
sushi
melon

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:11.580
Huh?
sushi
melon

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:12.480
Huh?

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:15.540
Ah, it’s there, it’s there.
That’s it.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.000
Hmm? I guess this’ll do.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:21.470
What?!

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:25.240
Azuma-san, I believe in you...

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.490
That you can’t possibly lose.

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:27.980
But...

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:31.980
But, is if okay to use that?!

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.400
The next day

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:44.510
All right, then...

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:47.540
From now onwards, the 30th
newcomers’ finals will begin.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:51.750
The people assigned to the A group, quickly
go to your designated work places.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:53.360
That’s me!

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.020
Azuma!

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.310
Win this one.

00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:00.450
Rock!

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:03.720
You moron! This isn’t rock-paper-scissors.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:05.610
You really are...

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:08.720
Azuma’s tendency to be out of it
just continues to increase.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.450
Ah, that hurt.

00:13:09.450 --> 00:13:10.240
Oh, I’m sorry...

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:13.020
Oh, no. I’m sorry, too.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.480
Motohashi

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:14.790
Oh, no. I’m sorry, too.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:25.240
Hey...

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:27.840
You’ll remember the promise, right?

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:28.740
Hmm?

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:32.450
If I win, you’d better address Tsukino as “nee-chan.”

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.270
Whatever...

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:39.000
And Kazu-kun, if you lose, you’ll
be my employee, all right?

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.510
Everyone is at their stations, right?

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:49.260
Well then, the first round of the finals
for the A group... hereby begins!

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:55.950
By the way, miss...

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:56.730
Yes?

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.750
What was it that Azuma bought?

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:02.540
Umm, that was... umm...

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.740
Huh? What, you think that I
might copy it or something?

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:09.720
I wasn’t thinking of something like that at all.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:11.780
Because...
what Azuma-san bought was...

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.810
Can you win with something like that?

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:20.150
Who knows...

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.010
W-What?

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:30.450
Amazing...

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.700
That looks like a really expensive melon...

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:36.810
It’s probably worth 100 times
the price of Azuma’s melon.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:40.910
This melon is of the highest grade, grown
through isolated bed cultivation.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:42.790
We use if sparingly at the store, but...

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:45.320
Today, we’ll go all the way, using only this pulp, 100%.

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.300
How very extravagant...

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.320
I want to eat it just like that...

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:55.550
To pulverize an expensive melon
like that...

00:14:55.550 --> 00:14:58.930
It’s something that could never have been
possible in my poverty stricken life.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:02.330
It’s something that’s definitely impossible
at the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:15:03.140 --> 00:15:07.820
Even without tasting it, we can tell that
it’ll be an extravagantly delicious bread.

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:10.630
I think the distance between that and Azuma’s item

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.700
is like the distance between heaven and earth, but...

00:15:12.700 --> 00:15:14.350
will it be all right, Azuma?

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:17.810
Huh... to have the time to be
worried about other people...

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.310
you sure have it easy there, Kawachi...

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.330
Suwabara!

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:24.560
But, aren’t you in the A group as well?

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:27.050
What happened to the match?

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.670
My opponent ran off in the middle
of the night for some reason.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.430
So, I won by default.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:36.340
Is that so?

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:38.270
He looks lonely from the back.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.140
What’s with him? He’s using two ovens!

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:44.250
Does he plan to make large quantities?

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:48.510
All right, while that’s being done...

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:02.020
Two ovens, eh?

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:05.520
I don’t know what the bluff is,

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:08.090
but it won’t work against me.

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:14.450
Two ovens...

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:24.930
It’s done.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:25.830
All right!

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:29.840
It looks like everyone in the A block is done, right?

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:31.840
I will begin the judging!

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.200
Victor: Atsumasu!

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:45.670
All right!

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:53.340
Huh? Kuroyanagi’s encouraging the loser!

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:54.610
He’s not going to call him trash, eh?

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:58.090
I guess finals participants
are really different.

00:16:58.090 --> 00:17:01.120
Even if they’ve lost, they’re amongst
the top 30 of the newcomers.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:04.970
Trash, trash, trash, trash, trash.
Go back. Trash, trash, trash...

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:07.630
Please spare me...

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:09.440
Next!

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.900
Yo, welcome.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:12.150
Yo, welcome.

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:13.090
Wha...?

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:17.820
Yo, welcome. The old... the young sir over there.

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:19.070
What will you have?

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:20.030
What are you trying to pull?

00:17:20.030 --> 00:17:22.920
However, asking that isn’t much good,
as we only have melon bread.

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:25.410
I’m asking you what you’re trying to pull!

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.020
What? Melon bread?

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:29.540
This is...?

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:32.030
All right, then. One melon bread coming up...

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:36.800
W-What the?

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:38.030
Azuma-san, what are you...?

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:44.540
Combine!

00:17:52.310 --> 00:17:53.230
All right, sorry for the wait!

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:55.740
One melon bread, all done.

00:17:56.610 --> 00:17:59.150
Sushi? That’s the answer to the sushi?

00:17:59.150 --> 00:18:00.970
That’s the melon sushi bread?

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:03.070
This is melon bread?

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:06.430
He joined the earlier pieces together, almost like sushi...

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:10.040
Another outrageous bread...

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:11.480
Hmm? This is...

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.420
He’s baked the cookie and bread separately,

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:17.090
and put melon-colored cream in the middle, eh?

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:20.280
But, why do something so troublesome?

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.790
If I let down my guard here, I’ll suffer damage again.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.100
All right.

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:29.780
Let’s go.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.340
O-Oh no!

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:39.970
I guess it came, after all!

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:53.800
MELON!!

00:18:57.710 --> 00:18:59.920
This is how he paints its deliciousness, eh?

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.780
There’ve been times I’ve thrown my head back,

00:19:02.510 --> 00:19:04.830
but to think that it’s to this extent...

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:08.810
Melon bread is made by simultaneously
baking the cookie dough,

00:19:08.810 --> 00:19:13.270
which takes time to bake, and the bread dough,
which requires only a third of the time to bake.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:17.480
Because of that, it’s always a little underbaked, and you get a sticky consistency.

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:20.070
This is even called the incomplete
portion of melon bread,

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:24.850
and many artisans have tried to aim for
its completion and piled on failures,

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:27.220
but now, truly, an answer to it has...

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.730
A perfect melon bread is here!

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.190
Also known as <i>Japan</i> #58.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:36.440
I don’t know of such a silly name.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:37.790
How mean...

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:40.880
This is why you used two ovens earlier, right?

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:41.450
Yeah.

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:44.090
To bake the cookie dough and the bread dough,

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:46.140
which have different baking times, in separate ovens...

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:49.180
and to put melon-flavored cream
in between as if it were wasabi,

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:51.770
piling them together like sushi!!

00:19:54.390 --> 00:19:56.820
Victor: Azuma Kazuma!

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.300
Hang on, time out!

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.800
You still haven’t tasted my melon bread!

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:08.430
If it’s the New Tokyo Branch’s melon bread,
then I’ve tasted it many times.

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:11.290
There’s no need to try it again now.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:12.830
That’s not right!

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:15.670
This melon bread’s made with
the highest grade muskmelon,

00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:19.540
with a sugar content of over 15%
and costing 15,000 apiece.

00:20:19.540 --> 00:20:23.510
Also, I’m using twice the amount of pulp that
we use for the melon bread in the store.

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:28.260
It’s obviously <i>much</i> more delicious than the
standard bread in the New Tokyo Branch.

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:30.170
Ah. It must be really delicious.

00:20:30.170 --> 00:20:31.910
See? You think so, right?

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:33.600
However!

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:35.620
It’s the <i>melon</i> that’s delicious!

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:39.070
Challenge him with the bread!

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:43.740
Azuma-san...

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:44.880
Mizuno!

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:49.320
You had promised. Address Tsukino as “nee-chan.”

00:20:49.320 --> 00:20:50.390
Azuma-san...

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:54.580
Okay.

00:20:54.580 --> 00:20:56.160
I’ll address her like that,

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:59.610
so in return, come to the New Tokyo Branch, Kazu-kun.

00:21:00.210 --> 00:21:01.920
I’ll pay you twice what you receive now.

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.090
Moreover, I’ll fawn all over you.

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:05.660
I don’t need those things!

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:09.050
I have the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:10.870
I’m perfectly happy with that.

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:15.870
Is that woman really that good?

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:19.950
You’re an idiot!

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:22.010
Hey, wait!

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:27.780
I’ll have my Koala-chan take my revenge for me,

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:29.660
so until then, the promise is on hold!

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:31.370
Hey!

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:33.240
Don’t just change the promise like that!

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:34.580
It’s all right, Azuma-san.

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:37.000
Tsukino! But...

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.870
It’s already settled with Azuma-san
not having to go anywhere.

00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:41.480
It’s enough with just that...

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:48.050
But if she doesn’t keep her promise then,
what we talked about in the beginning...

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:49.220
That’s true, but...

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:52.390
to think that the melon cream made from

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:57.460
the 120 yen can of melon juice surpassed
the pulp from the 15,000 yen melon...

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:01.500
When Tsukino told me, I thought he was a moron...

00:22:01.980 --> 00:22:04.270
But imagination’s the mother of bread.

00:22:04.270 --> 00:22:06.970
It’s not something so cheap as to
be created just for a higher price.

00:22:07.820 --> 00:22:09.450
By the way, Kawachi...

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:11.300
Are things all right over at your end?

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:13.580
Melon bread’s a specialty of mine.

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:17.620
In addition, I now have these Solar Gauntlets.

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:19.020
I’m invincible!

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:29.180
That’s not a tool to satisfy your self-conceit, Kawachi!

00:22:54.480 --> 00:22:56.240
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:56.240 --> 00:22:58.360
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:58.360 --> 00:23:00.360
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:01.660
The answer for now is...

00:23:01.660 --> 00:23:04.580
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:04.580 --> 00:23:06.370
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:08.160
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:18.260
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:18.260 --> 00:23:21.140
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:23.180
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:24.590
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:26.270 --> 00:23:29.390
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:31.230
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.780
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:53.710 --> 00:23:57.590
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:07.050
Next, it’s my turn!

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:09.400
It’s easy going with my Solar Gauntlets.

00:24:09.400 --> 00:24:10.690
Don’t let down your guard, Kawachi!

00:24:10.690 --> 00:24:13.610
Your opponent possesses “a mother’s hand!”

00:24:13.610 --> 00:24:14.700
What?!

00:24:14.700 --> 00:24:16.160
Next time on Yakitate Japan.

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:16.990
Delii-cious!!

00:24:16.990 --> 00:24:18.580
The trap of the yakisoba bread!

00:24:18.580 --> 00:24:20.020
Be sure to see it!

00:24:20.240 --> 00:24:22.770
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:25.920
Mizuno’s highest grade melon is grown
by isolated bed cultivation.

00:24:25.920 --> 00:24:28.750
It’s an amazing cultivation technique, so,
I’d like to explain in detail, but...

00:24:28.750 --> 00:24:30.380
even I find it impossible in 15 seconds.

00:24:30.380 --> 00:24:31.790
Check up on it yourself!

00:24:31.790 --> 00:24:33.680
Huh!?
